# Release Engineering Workflow

Full policy: `docs/RELEASE_ENGINEERING_WORKFLOW.md`  
Hardening notes: `docs/releases/RELEASE-ENGINEERING-HARDENING.md`

## Source of truth

`main` and `origin/main` only. Feature branches are temporary.

## Canonical deploy entry

```bash
sudo bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh deploy full
bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh verify-release
```

Never deploy feature branches, dirty trees, or local-only commits.

## Lifecycle

Architecture Review → Implementation → Tests → Review → Fixes → Acceptance → Merge `main` → Validate → Push `origin/main` → Deploy → Verify

## Hard rules

- Never merge or `git push origin main` without explicit user approval (ask separately).
- Never use `ALLOW_DIRTY_SYNC` / `DEPLOY_LOCAL_MAIN` for normal work (emergency only).
- Identity chain must match: origin/main == build-info == frontend identity == /api/build.
